  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">During the spring of 1991, I took daily walks over roads and paths along irrigation ditches in the Rio Grande valley near Albuquerque. On these walks numerous moments occurred during which natural phenomena created connections with each other or with my own thoughts. Some of these connections occurred again and again in the same place, while others were significant but singular. I began the Witness Post Project as a result of these walks. To honor the natural world and to mark sites of insight, connection or confluene in the landscape, I make witness posts out of various objects found on my walks. When placed in the landscape, the posts themselves become unexpected occurances and chances for connection with other walkers--colophon. Printed Matter.</subfield>
